- $\left(\sqrt{\frac{5}{2}}, \sqrt{\frac{5}{2}}\right)$ and $\left(-\sqrt{\frac{5}{2}}, -\sqrt{\frac{5}{2}}\right)$ are the intersection points on the positive x and the negative x axes, respectively.

