3 & & \times &   &   &   &   &   &   &    &   &    &   &   &   &   &   &   &  &  \\
7 & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & & &  &  \\
\end{array}
\]

To produce the first 20 positive integers that are relatively prime to 7: $\{1,3,5,2,4,6,2,3,5,2,4,6,2,3,5,2,4,6,2,3\}$, noting that there are only 10 distinct numbers in this list due to repetitions.

The smallest positive integer, $n$, that is greater than 1 and relatively prime to 7 is $2$, which is the first remaining number in the initial list that is marked with a check.

