\textbf{Solution:} First, let's find the factors of $243$:
\begin{align*}
243 &= 3^3 \cdot 7 \\
&= (3 \cdot 3 \cdot 3) \cdot (7) \\
\implies 13 &= 3 \cdot 3 \cdot 1 \\
\implies 15 &= 3 \cdot 5 \\
\end{align*}

Now, we need the product of $13$ and $15$ to be $243$, so we form the equation:
\begin{align*}
3 \cdot 3 \cdot 1 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 &= 3^3 \cdot 7 \\
\iff 9 \cdot 15 &= 243
\end{align*}

To make the product of $15$ and $9$ equal to $243$, we want the value of $15$'s factor to be a multiple of $9$. There's only one factor of $15$ that's divisible by $9$: $9$.

Since $15 = 3 \cdot 5$, we want $15 = 9 \cdot q$ for some integer $q$. Solving, we get $q = 1.5$. Since we cannot have a fraction, we must round $q$ down to the closest integer: $q = 1$.

So, $15 = 9 \cdot 1$. Hence, we need $b = 1$.

