Of this remaining area, the larger triangles, which are not entirely occupied by the smaller triangles, comprise only a fraction that corresponds to the ratio of the larger side length (which is 16 times the side length of the smaller triangles) to the sum of the larger side length and the (gaps between) smaller triangles, which is the sum of 45 smaller side lengths.

