\boxed{ 2pi(3mm)((\frac{Volume}{pi(3mm)^2}) + 3mm) }

Next, we substitute the expression for $h$ into the formula for the volume: $V = \pi r^{2} h$. Solving for the volume: $V = \pi r^{2} (\frac{V}{\pi r^{2}})$ which means the volume squared is equal to the area of the base of the cylinder. Thus, $V = \sqrt{\pi(3mm)^{2}}=\sqrt{\pi}*9mm^{2}$ which gives us:

