n & = (34.375^\circ)k \text{ where } k \ge 1\\
n & = 34.375^\circ + 34.375^\circ 2 + \cdots + 34.375^\circ (k-1)\\
n & = 34.375^\circ\sum\limits_{i = 1}^{k}i\\
\end{align*}

Since $0 \le n \le 180,$ we need to find the smallest integer $k$ such that $n \le 180.$

If we compute the sum $\sum\limits_{i = 1}^{5}i,$ we obtain $15,$ which is less than $180.$ However, if we compute the sum $\sum\limits_{i = 1}^{6}i,$ we obtain $21,$ which is greater than $180.$ Thus, the smallest integer $k$ that satisfies the condition $n \le 180$ is $k = 5.$

Therefore, the integer $n$ we are looking for is:

\begin{align*}
n & = (34.375^\circ)5 \ \approx \ 171.875^\circ\\
n &\approx 172^\circ \ \text{rounding to the nearest integer}
\end{align*}

