1. Since the triangles are congruent, the height $OP$ is the same in each triangle, so we can calculate it based on one triangle. Using the properties of an isosceles triangle, the altitude (height $OP$) is half of the base ($AB$), so:

   OP = (AB) / 2 = 12 / 2 = \boxed{\mathbf{6}}
2. Since the base $BC$ and height $OP$ for the trapezoid are known, we can find the area of the trapezoid using this formula:

   Area(trap) = (base1 + base2) * (height) / 2 = (12 + 12) * \boxed{6} / 2 = \boxed{36 \text{ units}^2}

So the area of the trapezoid (ABCD) is 36 square units.

